    text This function supports dynamic execution of Python code. must be either a string or a code object. If it is a string, the string is parsed as a suite of Python statements which is then executed (unless a syntax error occurs). If it is a code object, it is simply executed. In all cases, the code that’s executed is expected to be valid as file input (see the section in the Reference Manual). Be aware that the , , and statements may not be used outside of function definitions even within the context of code passed to the function. The return value is . @17,17194,663,121
