    text In all cases, if the optional parts are omitted, the code is executed in the current scope. If only globals is provided, it must be a dictionary (and not a subclass of dictionary), which will be used for both the global and the local variables. If globals and locals are given, they are used for the global and local variables, respectively. If provided, locals can be any mapping object. Remember that at the module level, globals and locals are the same dictionary. @17,17618,663,102
    card @17,17732,663,143
      text Note @34,17747,629,20
      text When exec gets two separate objects as globals and locals, the code will be executed as if it were embedded in a class definition. This means functions and classes defined in the executed code will not be able to access variables assigned at the top level (as the “top level” variables are treated as class variables in a class definition). @34,17779,629,81
    text If the dictionary does not contain a value for the key , a reference to the dictionary of the built-in module is inserted under that key. Overriding can be used to restrict or change the available names, but this is a security mechanism: the executed code can still access all builtins. @17,17887,663,61
