    text is an optional string that specifies the mode in which the file is opened. It defaults to which means open for reading in text mode. Other common values are for writing (truncating the file if it already exists), for exclusive creation, and for appending (which on Unix systems, means that writes append to the end of the file regardless of the current seek position). In text mode, if is not specified, UTF-8 is used by default; if is disabled, is called to get the current locale encoding. (For reading and writing raw bytes use binary mode and leave unspecified.) The available modes are: @17,35746,663,122
